 "text": "Hey! How's everything going? A sketch is a quick rough drawing or blown off idea, often done in ink with a single pen. Pretty much, yes. A study is a detailed and careful drawing from life, often with several views of the subject. A sketchbook is the best place to start. Start with a simple rough drawing, then add layers of tone and texture with pencils, charcoal and ink. Focus on capturing the overall feeling of the scene, rather than tiny details. Pick a few key features to focus on and give them a lot of attention. You' got it. A study can take weeks or months, so don't rush it. Take your time, and it' look amazing.",
